{
  "dom_id": "step-q78063",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "If $y=|x+1|$, what are the coordinates of the minimum point on the graph?",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that $y=|x-a|$ is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $a$ units right.\n\nThe function $y=|x+1|$ has $a=-1.$ Therefore, it is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $1$ unit left.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14250789/assets/38532ccdd10c7a60f26fdf35c837376af799d7b024370e8b223cd61b7b18eb9d.png)\n\nLooking at the graph, we can see that the coordinates of the minimum point are $(-1,0).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
